  "figures": [
    {
      "filename": "dye_depth_time.png",
      "title": "Dye depth\u2013time evolution",
      "caption": "Simulations only: model analog of Wagner et al. Fig. 8. The measured-wave-forcing case contains simulated dye, not measured dye. Horizontal-mean concentration C*=H c/M\u2080 uses the time-zero integrated dye mass M\u2080, held fixed throughout evolution; a uniformly mixed column has C*=1. The blue curve is the independently checked depth enclosing 99% of positive horizontal-mean dye. Gray intervals have no computed profiles; the wind-plus-molecular-loss validity stop is labeled. No laboratory dye data are shown."
    },
    {
      "filename": "dye_transverse_sections.png",
      "title": "Fixed-x transverse dye sections",
      "caption": "Model analog of Wagner et al. Fig. 5, adapted to a shared logarithmic concentration scale C*=H c/M\u2080 from 0.01 to 200. True fixed-x slices at x=6 cm show the actual 12 cm crosswind domain and full 50 mm depth. Requested ages are 18.0,19.5,20.0,20.5,21.5 s; every panel labels its actual saved age, with exact times and slice indices in this manifest. No unsaved fields are interpolated, no domain is tiled, and no laboratory panels are included."
    }
  ],
